    "source_semantic_class": "other_normative_clinical_instruction",
    "title_or_context": "heart failure care. The graph shows NP levels fluctuating between \"Dry\" NP (low) and \"Wet\" NP (high). \"Wet\" NP is associated with \"NP variations\" and \"Increasing filling pressure\". \"Dry\" NP is associated with \"Stable clinical status\". The trajectory shows a peak during \"Hemodynamic congestion\" and \"Hospitalization\", followed by a decline. \"IV therapies\" and \"Oral therapies\" are indicated as interventions. A table below the graph provides details on the utility of NP levels in different settings."
